00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Kick (also known as Kick.com) is an Australian video livestreaming service.

13
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:54,000
It is operated by Kick Streaming Pty Ltd and backed by online casino
company Stake.com and streaming personality Trainwreckstv.

14
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Kick was founded in 2022 as a competitor to Twitch, with a focus on looser moderation, higher revenue shares for
streamers, and the inclusion of online gambling content which has been banned from other platforms.

15
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
In 2023, Kick made multiple high-profile deals with
streamers including Adin Ross and xQc.

16
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
In Q3 2025, StreamCharts listed Kick.com as the fourth most watched livestreaming platform
(among those monitored by the site) behind YouTube, TikTok, and Twitch.

17
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
From 2023 until the end of 2025, Kick was also the sponsor of
the Sauber Motorsport racing team in Formula One.

